  "description": "The Lightest, Fastest Alloy Full Suspension Bike in the World gets a full makeover with the ultra-capable EVO build. Still 18.4% lighter than the closest competitor and sharing geometry and kinematics from our downcountry-hungry Epic 8 EVO, the all-new Chisel Comp EVO delivers the performance you can feel and is spec’d for the ultimate downcountry experience.\n\nSPEED METAL: With D’Aluisio Smartweld technology, the Chisel Comp EVO boasts the lightest aluminum XC frameset in its class. Each highly manipulated frame tube features continuously varied wall thicknesses and shaping that deliver stiffness where you need it– for efficiency – and ride-smoothing compliance where you want it—for comfort and optimal control.\n\nUNMATCHED CAPABILITY: With a slew of trail-ready specs, including a bump up to 130mm of travel up front, the Chisel EVO eats up the chunk and feels right at home on the rough stuff. Advanced suspension kinematics, Ride Dynamics tuned suspension, and progressive geometry, can all be found in the Chisel Comp EVO, making it more than capable of handling big rides with confidence and speed.\n\nINCREDIBLE EFFICIENCY: The Chisel Comp EVO is the most efficient pedaling bike in its class, thanks to the utilization of geometry and kinematics that went into our Epic 8 EVO platform. The steep seat tube positions you in the optimal pedaling position to save energy for the long rips down. Honed anti-squat reduces pedal-bob. Put it together, and Chisel Comp EVO translates every watt applied to the pedals into maximum forward motion.\n\nSMOOTHER IS FASTER: We engineered a flex stay rear end for class-leading suspension performance while eliminating the extra weight and maintenance associated with pivots required in a traditional design. More common on carbon bikes, extensive field and lab testing proves that Chisel Comp EVO has achieved the impossible—the efficiency, control, and lightweight of a flex stay design in the advanced alloy.\n\nHYDROFORMED ALLOY: Chisel Comp EVO shaves extra material and weight with a one-piece hydroformed seat tube that integrates the seat tube pivot, main pivot, and BB shell. On a more traditional bike, the seat tube is typically just a \"tube\" with pivots and BB shell welded on.",
